# tools/c/ceiling_teeth_witness.rish -- a declared ceiling is read where it can refuse.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/c/ceiling_teeth_witness.rish
#
# WHY. A module names a maximum so the thing it bounds can never grow past it. The declaration is
# half of that promise; the other half is a line that READS the constant somewhere a caller can be
# turned away. Three reds fired in one room in four days, each a ceiling whose declaration stood
# further forward than its enforcement -- %678, a count declared in hits and enforced in bytes;
# %688, a store's ceiling in bytes against a weave's in lines with the conversion nowhere; and the
# row of 20260910.043900, a document identified by its lines so the byte it ends with had no home.
# A lantern that fires twice becomes a loom.
#
# THE ONE GATE, at zero: a ceiling nothing reads. On the seating lap
# mantra/recall_subscribe_poll.rye declared max_mirror_pairs = 4 directly above the PeerBoltPair
# struct it was drawn for, and poll_one_cycle walked pairs.len with no ceiling anywhere, then cast
# that length to u32 unchecked. Declared and read by nothing in any tracked .rye -- which reads to
# a person exactly like a ceiling that holds, and is the whole shape of this class.
#
# ONE RATCHET, under a ceiling that only falls: asserted_only, where the strongest reading a file
# gives its own ceiling is an assert. An assert is a postcondition and a fine thing to keep; what
# it cannot do is turn a caller away, and a release build removes it. It ratchets rather than walls
# because a repair lands there, and a wall would refuse honest work in the same breath as a fault.
#
# WHY ONE GATE AND FIVE REPORTS. unread is decidable with no judgment: the constant appears once in
# its own file and nowhere else in the tree. Every other class asks what a line is FOR, and this
# scan answers that lexically, which is a proxy. Precedent one room over, and it is why this guard
# reaches for the narrow gate: tools/fixtures/c/ceiling_pair_scan.sh measured four lexical
# discriminators for its own class on 20260910 and every one leaked, so it stopped guessing and
# asked the file to declare itself.
#
# THE ROOMS ARE ARGUMENTS. Two readings stand: mantra and tally, walked constant by constant on the
# seating lap, and glow, adopted 20260917. Each carries its own assert-only ratchet in the scan's
# own `case`. Another lane adopts by naming itself there and reading what it inherits.
#
# WHAT IT DOES NOT REACH. Whether a refusal's threshold is the RIGHT number, which is the pair
# scan's subject and, past it, arithmetic. Whether a cut truncates something a caller needed whole.
# A ceiling declared const rather than pub const, since a private bound is the module's own
# business. And every language beside Rye.
#
# THE REFUSAL IS READ BY BLOCK, NEVER BY A LINE COUNT (REDS `20260917.040203`). The scan read three
# lines forward from the condition until this lap, and that window failed in both directions at
# once. It MISSED this tree's own growing idiom -- a refusal record filled between the test and the
# return -- so glow/tokens.rye refuses four ceilings with error.BadToken eleven lines below the test
# and every one read asserted_only, the ratchet: the repair that made those refusals diagnosable
# RAISED the meter. And it ADMITTED a refusal spelled in PROSE, since the condition test matches
# `and ` and a comment is a line. Twelve missed and two admitted, tree-wide, one root. Strings are
# blanked before comments, the condition's header closes at its parentheses, and the body is walked
# by brace depth to its matching close.
#
# GLOW READS ITS OWN NUMBER. The language lane adopts here at asserted_only <= 3, seated beside
# mantra and tally's 1 rather than merged with it, so a repair in one room can never pay for a
# regression in another. Adoption was unreachable before the block reading, since four of glow's
# five assert-only readings were the window missing a record.
#
# Pen: tools/fixtures/c/ceiling_teeth_control.sh -- thirty-one assertions across twenty-three behaviors
# on real Rye sources in a real git repository, every refusal planted and then lifted, the ratchet
# shown from both sides, and the repair proven to leave the population rather than stay in it.

say "ceiling-teeth: Language EN -- a ceiling is declared in one line and kept in another, and this reads the second."
say "ceiling-teeth: Style Gauge, Meter -- every count below is the scan's own output, read from the tree rather than recited here."
say "ceiling-teeth: Lens TAME -- bound everything, check at the edge, fail with a named error; the corpus is discovered from the rooms rather than listed."

let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/c/ceiling_teeth_scan.sh" "mantra" "tally"]
say scan.out
assert scan.ok else "ceiling-teeth: a ceiling is read by nothing, or the assert-only population spread -- read the scan's own lines"
assert scan.out contains "verdict=ok" else "ceiling-teeth: the census must agree with itself"
assert scan.out contains "unread=0" else "ceiling-teeth: a ceiling nobody reads bounds nothing at all"
assert scan.out contains "asserted_only_ceiling=1" else "ceiling-teeth: the ratchet ceiling moved -- a raise is a deliberate hand, and this one is meant only to fall"
assert (scan.out contains "verdict=empty_corpus" == false) else "ceiling-teeth: a meter over no ceilings must say so rather than pass"
assert (scan.out contains "verdict=unread_ceiling" == false) else "ceiling-teeth: the one gate stands at zero"
assert (scan.out contains "verdict=asserted_spread" == false) else "ceiling-teeth: the assert-only population may shrink and may not spread"
assert (scan.out contains "ceilings_declaring=0" == false) else "ceiling-teeth: a reading over no ceilings would report clean while measuring nothing"

# GLOW READS ITS OWN NUMBER, rather than joining mantra and tally in one total. A merged ratchet
# lets a repair in one room pay for a regression in another, which is the hatch two gated numbers
# close; and the language lane could not adopt at all until 20260917, because four of glow's five
# assert-only readings were the three-line window missing a refusal record (REDS `20260917.040203`).
let glow = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/c/ceiling_teeth_scan.sh" "glow"]
say glow.out
assert glow.ok else "ceiling-teeth: glow declares a ceiling nothing reads, or its assert-only population spread"
assert glow.out contains "verdict=ok" else "ceiling-teeth: the glow census must agree with itself"
assert glow.out contains "unread=0" else "ceiling-teeth: a glow ceiling nobody reads bounds nothing at all"
assert glow.out contains "asserted_only_ceiling=3" else "ceiling-teeth: glow's ratchet ceiling moved -- a raise is a deliberate hand, and this one is meant only to fall"
assert (glow.out contains "ceilings_declaring=0" == false) else "ceiling-teeth: a reading over no glow ceilings would report clean while measuring nothing"

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/c/ceiling_teeth_control.sh"]
say control.out
assert control.ok else "ceiling-teeth: the control must complete"
assert control.out contains "control_fail=0" else "ceiling-teeth: every planted behavior must read as written"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "ceiling-teeth: the control must agree with itself"
assert control.out contains "1 free: a ceiling refused by name reads as refused -- ok" else "ceiling-teeth: the honest form must pass free"
assert control.out contains "2 free: a ceiling sizing an array reads as structural -- ok" else "ceiling-teeth: a bound the compiler holds is a bound"
assert control.out contains "3 free: a clamped value reads as cut -- ok" else "ceiling-teeth: a value clamped to its ceiling is bounded by construction"
assert control.out contains "4 free: a ceiling a second constant derives from reads as derived -- ok" else "ceiling-teeth: a derived ceiling carries its teeth where it is derived"
assert control.out contains "5 bitten: an assert-only population past its ceiling refuses -- ok" else "ceiling-teeth: the ratchet must bite from above"
assert control.out contains "6 free: the same population at exactly its ceiling passes free -- ok" else "ceiling-teeth: a ratchet must be a ceiling rather than a wall"
assert control.out contains "7 bitten: a ceiling nothing reads refuses -- ok" else "ceiling-teeth: the one gate must bite, or a declared ceiling can bound nothing in silence"
assert control.out contains "7 bitten: the refusal names the file and the constant -- ok" else "ceiling-teeth: a refusal naming neither leaves the reader to search"
assert control.out contains "8 free: the same ceiling given a named refusal leaves the population -- ok" else "ceiling-teeth: the repair must be rewarded rather than merely permitted"
assert control.out contains "9 free: a ceiling read by a sibling file is not unread -- ok" else "ceiling-teeth: a ceiling a caller reads is read"
assert control.out contains "10 free: a private const is not a declared ceiling -- ok" else "ceiling-teeth: a private bound is the module's own business"
assert control.out contains "11 free: a witness source is read past -- ok" else "ceiling-teeth: a witness bounds its own fixtures"
assert control.out contains "12 bitten: a reading over no ceilings says so rather than passing -- ok" else "ceiling-teeth: a meter over nothing must say so"
assert control.out contains "13 free: an honest file never masks an unread ceiling beside it -- ok" else "ceiling-teeth: one honest file must never hide a fault beside it"
assert control.out contains "14 free: a refusal record between the test and the return still reads as refused -- ok" else "ceiling-teeth: the record-filling refusal is this tree's own idiom and must read as one"
assert control.out contains "15 bitten: the same block without a named-error return leaves refused -- ok" else "ceiling-teeth: the block walk must read the return rather than the distance"
assert control.out contains "16 bitten: a ceiling named only in a comment is not refused by the return below it -- ok" else "ceiling-teeth: prose is not a refusal"
assert control.out contains "17 free: the two-line braceless refusal reads as refused -- ok" else "ceiling-teeth: the braceless form keeps its place"
assert control.out contains "18 free: a multi-line condition closes at its parentheses -- ok" else "ceiling-teeth: a condition closes where its parentheses do, never after a guessed line count"
assert control.out contains "19 bitten: a return past the closing brace is not that ceiling's refusal -- ok" else "ceiling-teeth: a return outside the block belongs to the function rather than the test"
assert control.out contains "20 bitten: a ceiling named inside a string literal is not refused by that line -- ok" else "ceiling-teeth: an emitted source's own if is not this file's refusal"
assert control.out contains "M1 bitten: removing the string blanking admits a refusal spelled inside a literal -- ok" else "ceiling-teeth: the string blanking must be load-bearing"
assert control.out contains "M2 bitten: removing the comment stripping admits a refusal spelled in prose -- ok" else "ceiling-teeth: the comment stripping must be load-bearing"
assert control.out contains "M3 bitten: removing the block walk loses the refusal it was built to find -- ok" else "ceiling-teeth: the block walk must be load-bearing"

say "ceiling-teeth: GREEN -- every declared ceiling in mantra, tally and glow is read where it can refuse, and each room's assert-only population holds."
